Chapter: IdentitySetProcTest

 identity-set-proc writes another process's identity word. Its kernel
 helper tests two bits, so the intrinsic carries both Identity and
 Capability and the program declares both.

Section: Body
  child-body : Integer -> Integer
  child-body (x) = poke-byte 28000 0 (if identity-whoami 0 == 777 then 1 else 0)

  after-set : Integer, Integer -> Text
  after-set (pid) (s) =
    if s /= 0 then "FAIL: identity-set-proc returned error"
    else let wt = process-wait pid
    in if peek-byte 28000 0 == 1 then "PASS"
    else "FAIL: child did not see new identity"

  set-and-check : Integer -> [Identity, Capability] Text
  set-and-check (pid) = after-set pid (identity-set-proc pid 0 777)

  opening : [Console, Concurrent, Identity, Capability] Nothing = act
    pid <- process-spawn (\x -> child-body x)
    print-line-uni (set-and-check pid)
  end
